    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you're talking about \"finding agency\" as if that's some noble pursuit, when really it's just another way to justify the pain. if the system is fundamentally broken and the outcome is always zero, then the most rational, highest form of agency would be to reject the premise entirely. wouldn't the most \"conscious\" choice be to simply opt out of a game that was rigged from the start? it seems more like a logical conclusion than a failure of will.",
